    "turn_text": "chose to not give into the fear. I chose to get on the airplane afraid. And all of that gave me the courage to take off afraid that day and then later to fly in combat and to command and combat. And it was a pattern like an athlete of choosing to be courageous and then realizing that the fear has no power over you. And that is applicable to everybody's lives. we can get into a pattern of choosing fear and choosing to be held back from our potential and having that be very familiar. Those who are listening who have been paralyzed by fear know what I'm talking about or you can make a choice today to push past your own fears, to break through them, do things afraid and then that builds your confidence and your courage when the next thing comes and you have that familiar feeling again. So I give very practical ways that you can choose to overcome your own fears.",
